<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NB - no buyer T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	 MONTH	 PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	   30/25 D	 April	  27/28 D</p>
<p> May	     28/25 D	 May	    17/13 D</p>
<p> July	    21/15 D	 July	    10/5 D</p>
<p> August	  12/20 P	 August	 15/25 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	 MONTH	 PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	   21 D/NS	 April	  19/17 D</p>
<p> May	 19.5/18.5 D	 May	16.5/15.5 D</p>
<p> July	19.5/18.5 D	 July     16.5/15.5 D</p>
<p> August	  8/7.5 D	 August	even/3 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	  BASIS	 MONTH	 PREVIOUS</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed) Fob Paranagua  April	   50 D/NS	 April	130/110 D</p>
<p> May	     90 D/NS	 May	  130/110 D</p>
<p> July	   100/70 D	 July	 130/110 D</p>
<p> August	 100/70 D	 August	110/80 D</p>
<p>Note: The next price message will be on May 2 due to the Labor Day holiday Thursday.</p>
</text>
